Changelog:
Version 2.1.0
1) fixed chrome.storage.sync per-window 8KB quota errors: favicon data: URIs
   (often several KB each) are no longer persisted, and windows that are
   still too large are transparently split across multiple sync keys
2) added a first-run onboarding banner explaining the new local sync and
   offering a one-click check/import of the old TabCloud cloud account
3) added a persistent "Migration info" link and a "synced locally" badge so
   it's always clear which storage is in use
Version 2.0.0
1) migrated to Manifest V3 (service worker background, chrome.storage.local)
2) replaced the chrometabcloud.appspot.com cloud sync with chrome.storage.sync
   (no server dependency); added a one-time optional import from the old
   TabCloud cloud account in the options page
Version 1.1.0
1) imported TabCloud plugin
2) added window tracking feature. 
